##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
We adopt the resonance parameters from the existing               7531 1451
ENDF/B.VII evaluation. These used                                 7531 1451
the resolved resonance parameters taken directly from the         7531 1451
evaluation of Mughabghab [mug84] up to 2.0 keV                    7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       7531 1451
calculated with Talys. If the maximal cross section in an         7531 1451
excitation function over the whole energy range does not exceed   7531 1451
1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not included at all. Cross sections     7531 1451
lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have no physical meaning and   7531 1451
are set to zero. Not all of the following MT-numbers may be       7531 1451
present for this isotope, because this depends on Q-values.       7531 1451
They are all listed for completeness.                             7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
Above 2 keV, calculations from the spherical OMP were used.       7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    7531 1451
total cross section.                                              7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
For energies below 20 MeV, MT5 contains the lumped (n,gamma x)    7531 1451
cross section, where x may represent neutron, proton, deuteron,   7531 1451
triton, Helium-3 or alpha. Using the relative yields of MF6/MT5,  7531 1451
the (n,gamma n), (n,gamma p), ..., (n,gamma alpha) can be         7531 1451
recovered. These cross sections are relatively small. However,    7531 1451
addition of these cross sections, which can not be stored in any  7531 1451
other MT-number, ensures that the partial cross sections add up   7531 1451
to the non-elastic cross section. Above 20 MeV, MT5 contains the  7531 1451
total non-elastic cross section, with which the information of    7531 1451
MF6/MT5 can be combined to obtain particle production cross       7531 1451
sections and (double-)differential cross sections.                7531 1451
                                                                  7531 1451
- MT11     : (n,2nd) cross section                                7531 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 7531 1451
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 7531 1451
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 7531 1451
